  "text_sanskrit": "सत्त्वं सुखे सञ्जयति रजः कर्मणि भारत । ज्ञानमावृत्य तु तमः प्रमादे सञ्जयत्युत ॥ १४-९ ॥",
  "itrans": "sattvaM sukhe sa~njayati rajaH karmaNi bhArata . j~nAnamAvR^itya tu tamaH pramAde sa~njayatyuta .. 14-9 ..",
  "translation": "Satva puts one into bliss; Rajas into action, O Bharata, whereas, Tamas enveloping knowledge puts one into heedlessness also.\nV. As before Satva, &c, denote both the matter and the deity. Also: includes indolence, &c Enveloping knowledge: obstructing the power of mind to know the truth. (9)\nA. If all the three Gunas form the cause of bondage in all cases, how is it that the effect of one particular Guna alone is seen in each case? In answer it is pointed out that the observation is due to the preponderance or the one or the other quality.",
